fresh-eyes: independent reviewer, the missouri composite action.

Exercised: YAML and composite schema parsed; git ls-remote shapes for a
branch, a missing branch, and an annotated tag; cargo's resolution of a
tag-object sha and of a bad rev; the exact install command against the
resolved main sha into a scratch root (exit 0, 1m19s, missouri 0.2.0
on PATH); Cargo.lock v4 tracked at main; no -sys crates, so a plain
cargo install builds on ubuntu-latest.

Two hardenings applied after review: the cache key carries runner.arch,
and the install step takes the sha through env instead of splicing an
expression into the script (the resolve step's own pattern).
